cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use substrata in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "substrata: 3-D point-cloud analysis for coral reef photogrammetry"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pim
    family-names: Bongaerts
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6747-6044"
    affiliation: "California Academy of Sciences"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/reefscapegenomics/substrata"
url: "https://substrata.readthedocs.io/"
abstract: >-
  substrata is a Python package and command-line tool for processing and
  analyzing 3-D reconstructions of coral reefs. It takes the outputs of a
  structure-from-motion pipeline (dense point clouds, camera poses, and image
  annotations) and turns them into scaled, oriented models that can be
  measured, annotated, and compared across sites, depths, and time points.
keywords:
  - photogrammetry
  - point cloud
  - structure from motion
  - coral reef
  - 3-D reconstruction
  - benthic ecology
